WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.820
A message from your bank:

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.540
the interest rate on
your savings has gone up.

3
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.510
Good news. Your money now grows faster,

4
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:09.450
just for sitting in the bank.

5
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.770
Rates can swing a long way.

6
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:16.460
The UK's central bank set
0.1 per cent in March 2020,

7
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.750
and 5.25 per cent by August 2023.

8
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.540
So if a bank pays you more for saving,

9
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.910
why might shops across the
country start to struggle?

10
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.570
In this mission, you'll
turn an interest rate dial

11
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.000
and watch what households do next.

12
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.430
Then you'll meet savers and borrowers,

13
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.470
and find out who wins and
who loses when rates change.

14
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.970
Your mission: explain how
one interest rate can change

15
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.040
spending across a whole country.
